<title>GERMANY: AGIV says expects improved 1996 results.</title>
<headline>AGIV says expects improved 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified industrial group AGIV AG said on Friday it expected to post improved results for 1996 after reporting a 4.8 percent increase in six-month sales and a gain in orders in hand.</p>
<p>The Frankfurt-based group said it expected &quot;clearly better&quot; results from its machinery building units, in part from the restructuring of its Barmag unit and positive new orders from its Carl Schenck subsidiary.</p>
<p>But the group said its results would be negatively impacted by a recession in the German construction industry.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
